# This repository is the canonical publication point for byte-exact artifacts:
# a third party vendors these files and pins their SHA-256, and two runtimes
# agree on them byte for byte. An end-of-line conversion on checkout would make
# a Windows clone and a Linux clone publish different bytes under one release
# tag, which is the one thing an immutable release may never do.
#
# The stored blobs are already LF; this only stops checkout from rewriting them.

# The released Public Evidence Packet schemas.
schema/** -text

# The commitment golden vectors (packet format 1.4.0, product PRUVZ-26).
commitment/** -text

# The trust-registry golden vectors (release 1.4.1, product PRUVZ-95).
trust-registry/** -text

# The evidence-log golden vectors (release 1.4.2, product PRUVZ-87).
evidence-log/** -text

# The anchoring golden vectors (release 1.4.3, product PRUVZ-96).
anchoring/** -text
